@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 # Telegram Messages
 
-Manage messages: send, edit, delete, forward, pin, react, search, and browse history.
+Manage messages: send, edit, delete, forward, pin, react, search, browse history,
+and read inline-button taps.
 
 ## Actions
 
@@ -10,6 +11,22 @@ Send a new message to a chat.
 - **text** (required): Message text
 - **reply_to**: Message ID to reply to
 - **parse_mode**: "HTML" or "Markdown"
+- **buttons**: Inline keyboard, as rows of `{"text": ..., "data": ...}` (bot mode only)
+
+```jsonc
+{
+  "action": "send",
+  "chat_id": 375465077,
+  "text": "DEC-12 — move \"pay the insurance\" to 24.10?",
+  "buttons": [[{"text": "✅ Yes",   "data": "DEC-12:yes"},
+               {"text": "✖️ No",    "data": "DEC-12:no"},
+               {"text": "🕓 Later", "data": "DEC-12:later"}]]
+}
+```
+
+`data` becomes the Bot API `callback_data` returned by the `callbacks` action.
+Limits enforced before the request goes out: `data` is 1-64 bytes (UTF-8), at
+most 8 buttons per row and 100 rows. A flat list is accepted as a single row.
 
 ### edit
 Edit an existing message.
@@ -17,6 +34,10 @@ Edit an existing message.
 - **message_id** (required): Message to edit
 - **text** (required): New text
 - **parse_mode**: "HTML" or "Markdown"
+- **buttons**: Replace the inline keyboard; `[]` strips it (bot mode only)
+
+Editing the text with `buttons: []` is the usual way to close a question:
+`"DEC-12 — … — ✅ yes"` with no buttons left to tap.
 
 ### delete
 Delete a message.
@@ -51,3 +72,46 @@ Get chat message history (user mode only).
 - **chat_id** (required): Chat ID or username
 - **limit**: Max messages (default: 20)
 - **offset_id**: Start from this message ID
+
+### callbacks
+Read inline-button taps since the last read (bot mode only).
+- **since_id**: Read updates after this `update_id`; omitted, the server's own
+  cursor is used
+- **limit**: Max updates per call, 1-100 (default: 20)
+- **ack_text**: Text shown in the tap confirmation toast
+- **strip_buttons**: Remove the keyboard from each answered message (default: false)
+
+```jsonc
+{"action": "callbacks", "since_id": 123456789, "limit": 50}
+```
+
+```jsonc
+{
+  "callbacks": [{"update_id": 123456790,
+                 "data": "DEC-12:yes",
+                 "from_id": 375465077,
+                 "chat_id": 375465077,
+                 "message_id": 4711,
+                 "date": "2026-08-25T14:03:11Z",
+                 "callback_query_id": "...",
+                 "answered": true}],
+  "count": 1,
+  "ignored": [],
+  "cursor": 123456790
+}
+```
+
+Every returned tap is acknowledged with `answerCallbackQuery`, so the client's
+spinner stops. `date` is the date of the message carrying the buttons -- the Bot
+API does not report the moment of the tap.
+
+**The cursor is server-side.** It advances past everything a call consumed, so
+calling `callbacks` twice never replays a tap the agent already acted on, and a
+restart does not rewind it (it is stored in `TELEGRAM_DATA_DIR`).
+
+**Taps are filtered before they reach you.** `TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_CALLBACK_SENDERS`
+(comma-separated user IDs) and `TELEGRAM_CALLBACK_DATA_PATTERN` (a regex, e.g.
+`^DEC-\d+:(yes|no|later)$`) decide what counts; anything else is logged, listed
+under `ignored`, and never acknowledged. With no allowlist configured, *any*
+Telegram user who reaches the bot can tap its buttons -- set it whenever the
+buttons drive real actions.
